{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Metropolitan Atlanta Rapid Transit Authority", "line": "Metropolitan Atlanta Rapid Transit Authority: Blue Line", "id": "marta-blue-line", "color": "#0092D0", "mode": "rapid_transit", "avg_speed_kmh": 40, "speed_source": "estimated typical MARTA heavy-rail operating speed (station stops included); unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1979, "end": 1993, "headway_min": 8, "note": "MARTA's first rail service: the East Line (Avondale-Georgia State) opened June 30 1979, followed by the West Line (Five Points-Hightower, now Hamilton E. Holmes) on Dec 22 1979, giving a single Hamilton E. Holmes-Avondale route (not yet reaching Indian Creek, shown here for continuity). Opening-day headway was 8 minutes per route.", "sources": ["Segment-level: this segment's own note carries the citation for its dates and service. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MARTA_rail", "https://www.itsmarta.com/"]}, {"start": 1993, "end": 2009, "headway_min": 8, "note": "Extended east beyond the I-285 perimeter to Kensington and Indian Creek June 26 1993, MARTA's first extension past the perimeter, completing the route shown here. Still known simply as the East-West Line before the 2009 color rebrand.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MARTA_rail", "https://www.itsmarta.com/"]}, {"start": 2009, "end": 2026, "headway_min": 11, "note": "Renamed the Blue Line Oct 1 2009 when MARTA switched from directional to color-coded line names. Modern scheduled headways vary by period (roughly 10 min peak, 12 min midday, 15 min weekends, 20 min nights); 11 min used here as a representative blend.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEV