33.76981], [-84.22665, 33.76974]]}}], "metadata": {"line_label_audit": "2026-08-24: line labels normalised repo-wide to \"<operating company>: <line name>\" -- the company's common display name (legal suffixes dropped), then the line as a passenger would have known it, or its two terminals where the line carried no advertised name. Long intermediate station lists were reduced to endpoints. For features spanning several operators the company shown is the one that ran the line for most of its drawn years. See CLAUDE.md Rule 6.", "sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MARTA_rail (MARTA heavy rail opened 1979; the North-South Line built in stages from 1981; the 2009 renaming to the colour-coded Red, Gold, Blue and Green line names and the Feb 2010 change of the Yellow Line to Gold after community feedback)", "https://www.itsmarta.com/ -- MARTA's own service information for present-day headways"], "not_yet_sourced": "Station-by-station opening dates quoted in the segment notes (Garnett-North Avenue Dec 4 1981, West End Sept 11 1982 and the rest) have NOT been individually verified against a source. Present-day headways are approximate and vary by period; they are not taken from a published timetable."}}